{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Parallel\" queries are queries that are executed in parallel, or at the same time so as to maximize fetching concurrency."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-parallel-queries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual Parallel Queries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the number of parallel queries does not change, there is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no extra effort"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to use parallel queries. Just use any number of TanStack Query's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectInfiniteQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" functions side-by-side!"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export class AppComponent {\n  // The following queries will execute in parallel\n  readonly usersQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['users'],\n    queryFn: fetchUsers,\n  }))\n  readonly teamsQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['teams'],\n    queryFn: fetchTeams,\n  }))\n  readonly projectsQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['projects'],\n    queryFn: fetchProjects,\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"dynamic-parallel-queries-with-injectqueries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Parallel Queries with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query provides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueries"},{"type":"text","value":", which you can use to dynamically execute as many queries in parallel as you'd like."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options object"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queries key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" whose value is an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array of query objects"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It returns an "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"array of query results"}]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export class AppComponent {\n  users = signal<Array<User>>([])\n\n  // Please note injectQueries is under development and this code does not work yet\n  readonly userQueries = injectQueries(() => ({\n    queries: users().map((user) => {\n      return {\n        queryKey: ['user', user.id],\n        queryFn: () => fetchUserById(user.id),\n      }\n    }),\n  }))\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using TypeScript, an inline "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" written on a query object passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" can't infer its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" argument from that same object's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" — it falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":". Annotate the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter explicitly, or define the query with the "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/functions/queryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" helper, to keep type inference. See "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/issues/6556","children":[{"type":"text","value":"this known limitation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"manual-parallel-queries","text":"Manual Parallel Queries","level":2},{"id":"dynamic-parallel-queries-with-injectqueries","text":"Dynamic Parallel Queries with injectQueries","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n\"Parallel\" queries are queries that are executed in parallel, or at the same time so as to maximize fetching concurrency.\n\n## Manual Parallel Queries\n\nWhen the number of parallel queries does not change, there is **no extra effort** to use parallel queries. Just use any number of TanStack Query's `injectQuery` and `injectInfiniteQuery` functions side-by-side!\n\n\n\n```ts\nexport class AppComponent {\n  // The following queries will execute in parallel\n  readonly usersQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['users'],\n    queryFn: fetchUsers,\n  }))\n  readonly teamsQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['teams'],\n    queryFn: fetchTeams,\n  }))\n  readonly projectsQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['projects'],\n    queryFn: fetchProjects,\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n## Dynamic Parallel Queries with `injectQueries`\n\n\n\nTanStack Query provides `injectQueries`, which you can use to dynamically execute as many queries in parallel as you'd like.\n\n\n\n\n`injectQueries` accepts an **options object** with a **queries key** whose value is an **array of query objects**. It returns an **array of query results**:\n\n\n\n\n```ts\nexport class AppComponent {\n  users = signal<Array<User>>([])\n\n  // Please note injectQueries is under development and this code does not work yet\n  readonly userQueries = injectQueries(() => ({\n    queries: users().map((user) => {\n      return {\n        queryKey: ['user', user.id],\n        queryFn: () => fetchUserById(user.id),\n      }\n    }),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n\n\n\n> When using TypeScript, an inline `select` written on a query object passed to `injectQueries` can't infer its `data` argument from that same object's `queryFn` — it falls back to `unknown`. Annotate the `select` parameter explicitly, or define the query with the [`queryOptions`](../reference/functions/queryOptions.md) helper, to keep type inference. See [this known limitation](https://github.com/TanStack/query/issues/6556).\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: parallel-queries\ntitle: Parallel Queries\nref: docs/framework/react/guides/parallel-queries.md\nreplace:\n  {\n    'If the number of queries you need to execute is changing from render to render, you cannot use manual querying since that would violate the rules of hooks. Instead, ': '',\n    'hook': 'function',\n    'React': 'Angular',\n    'hooks': 'functions',\n    'useQuery': 'injectQuery',\n    'useInfiniteQuery': 'injectInfiniteQuery',\n    'useQueries': 'injectQueries',\n  }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n\n```ts\nexport class AppComponent {\n  // The following queries will execute in parallel\n  readonly usersQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['users'],\n    queryFn: fetchUsers,\n  }))\n  readonly teamsQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['teams'],\n    queryFn: fetchTeams,\n  }))\n  readonly projectsQuery = injectQuery(() => ({\n    queryKey: ['projects'],\n    queryFn: fetchProjects,\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example'\n[//]: # 'Info'\n[//]: # 'Info'\n[//]: # 'DynamicParallelIntro'\n\nTanStack Query provides `injectQueries`, which you can use to dynamically execute as many queries in parallel as you'd like.\n\n[//]: # 'DynamicParallelIntro'\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n\n```ts\nexport class AppComponent {\n  users = signal<Array<User>>([])\n\n  // Please note injectQueries is under development and this code does not work yet\n  readonly userQueries = injectQueries(() => ({\n    queries: users().map((user) => {\n      return {\n        queryKey: ['user', user.id],\n        queryFn: () => fetchUserById(user.id),\n      }\n    }),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n[//]: # 'Example2'\n"}
